  "slug": "astrometric-precision-incoherent-4af7",
  "summary": "New analyses pit w0wa, early dark energy and primordial-feature models against DESI BAO, Planck PR4, HSC-Y3 shear, FRBs and JWST galaxy counts.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is testing whether combined datasets prefer extensions of ΛCDM, chiefly dynamical dark energy. HSC-Y3 cosmic shear with DESI BAO, DES SNe and BBN priors yields a 2.4σ preference for time-varying w. Allowing w0wa removes the hinted early-recombination preference from CMB+BAO and gives the lowest AIC. A genetic-algorithm reconstruction of scalar-tensor Lagrangians improves on ΛCDM by Δχ²=-16.6. 125 localized FRBs alone constrain Ω_m and w for the first time. A Bayesian forecast asks whether Simons Observatory and CMB-S4 can separate w0waCDM from ΛCDM shadow models. On H0, a double-power scalar field unifies early and late dark energy, and axion EDE with JWST high-redshift galaxy abundances gives H0≈72.76 km/s/Mpc. Searches for axion monodromy and full-shape BOSS/eBOSS oscillatory features find no significant evidence. Updated CMB acoustic priors separate early-Universe information from lensing and ISW. Separately, NANOGrav binary pulsars constrain ultralight dark matter couplings.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
